<!-- ============ THE E-COMMERCE MISSION ============ -->
<!-- The copy always said there are two opposed missions. The old layout was four
     stat cards, which expressed neither of them. Now the two failure modes face
     each other and converge on the one number that fixes both. -->
<section class="ac-purple sunk emx">
  <div class="emx-glow"></div>
  <div class="container" style="position: relative; z-index: 1;">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">The E-Commerce Mission</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Two missions that pull in opposite directions.</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Never promise what you do not have. Never fail to offer what you do. Miss either one and the cost lands on the same customer.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="emx-pair">
      <div class="emx-mission">
        <span class="emx-num">Mission 01</span>
        <h3>When the site oversells</h3>
        <p class="emx-lead">The site sells a unit the shelf does not have.</p>
        <ul class="emx-cost">
          <li><i class="ti ti-x"></i> The order is canceled after the customer has paid</li>
          <li><i class="ti ti-x"></i> A refund, an apology, and a shopper who now doubts the stock figure</li>
          <li><i class="ti ti-x"></i> Every subsequent promise on the site is worth less</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="emx-vs" aria-hidden="true"><span>and</span></div>

      <div class="emx-mission">
        <span class="emx-num">Mission 02</span>
        <h3>When the shelf goes unsold</h3>
        <p class="emx-lead">The shelf holds a unit the site will not sell.</p>
        <ul class="emx-cost">
          <li><i class="ti ti-x"></i> Stock sits in a stockroom while the page reads sold out</li>
          <li><i class="ti ti-x"></i> The sale goes to whoever did trust their own numbers</li>
          <li><i class="ti ti-x"></i> The markdown at the end of the season is yours to take</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="emx-converge" aria-hidden="true">
      <span></span><span></span>
    </div>

    <div class="emx-fix">
      <div class="emx-fix-head">
        <span class="emx-fix-eyebrow"><i class="ti ti-check"></i> Both come down to one number</span>
        <h3>Available-to-Sell your e-commerce can actually trust.</h3>
        <p>Available-to-Sell is calculated from what the system believes is on hand. Counting the floor by EPC, often, is what makes that belief true, so the number your website is selling against matches the shelf.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

